# Spec-Kit + Hybrid workflow

This repository uses the Umbrella Spec-Kit lifecycle together with the
portable Hybrid workflow. Treat the following as the operational command map:

- `/speckit.start` starts a work item only from a clean Git worktree and records
  `base_ref`.
- `/speckit.specify` creates the feature contract; `/speckit.clarify` closes
  decisions before plan.
- `/speckit.plan` and `/speckit.tasks` operate on the canonical full-mode
  `specs/<work-item>/spec.md`; run
  `bash workflow/core/check-workflow-contract.sh --task-spec <spec.md>` before
  implementation.
- `/speckit.analyze` is a blocking consistency and source-of-truth audit before
  implementation.
- `/speckit.implement` follows the replaceable `workflow/project/` adapter.
- `/speckit.hybrid-finalize` is the delivery gate. It must finish with exit code
  0 and a report containing the required evidence markers.

For new high-risk work items, declare
`CONTRACT_RECONCILIATION: required` and, when authorization has independent
actor/outcome branches, `AUTH_MATRIX_ROW_COVERAGE: required`. The core checks
the declarations and evidence shape; the product adapter checks technology-
specific named assertions and current runtime proof.

Before claiming READY, commit only the allowlisted implementation and run the
Hybrid finalizer on a clean worktree. A workflow-only pass confirms only this
workflow installation and is never product delivery evidence.

Codex/API prompts are under `.codex/prompts`, Codex project skills are under
`.agents/skills`, and this rule keeps the same command contract visible to
Cursor sessions. В этом репозитории есть только проверки самого workflow;
перед использованием в продукте замените `workflow/project/` адаптером с
реальными технологическими проверками.
